cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Pandemic guidelines: Delphi analysis and review synthesis"
message: >-
  If you use this software, cite the paper it belongs to. Cite this
  record for the software itself.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/lstell21/pg-delphi-analysis"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for an expert Delphi study on infectious disease
  modelling for pandemic preparedness. Computes the consensus
  statistics, derives theme coverage over the reviewed literature,
  and builds every table and figure in the paper.
keywords:
  - Delphi study
  - infectious disease modelling
  - pandemic preparedness
  - consensus methods
  - systematic review
authors:
  - family-names: Stellbrink
    given-names: Leonard
    affiliation: University of Luebeck
    email: leonard.stellbrink@uni-luebeck.de
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Preparing for the Next Pandemic Takes More Than Better Models:
    Expert Consensus Recommendations for Infectious Disease Modelling
  authors:
    - family-names: Stellbrink
      given-names: Leonard
